<title>USA: Hilton partner propose casino in S. Africa.</title>
<headline>Hilton partner propose casino in S. Africa.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hilton Hotels Corp. and Johnnies Industrial Corp. Ltd. of South Africa have submitted a proposal to build a $438 million hotel-casino in the Gauteng Province of South Africa, Hilton said Sunday.</p>
<p>In a statement, Hilton said a proposal was made to the Gauteng Gambling and Betting Board calling for a 432-room hotel with a 107,640-square-foot casino. The casino would have 71 table games and 2,000 slot machines.</p>
<p>The project also would include a 7,500-seat arena and 1,200-seat showroom.</p>
<p>The complex, would be called Bally's Hotel and Casino at Gallagher Estate.</p>
